        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "words": 72,
      "text": "So, the first rock is the [Pillar] of Glory, the Perfect Man, which was summoned [by the] glorious Ambassador. He set it in this zone; [ ... he] brought forth its base (?) from the earth to heaven. It bore up under the [en]tire uni[verse], and became first of all the weight-carriers in [it]s powers. In its firmness it has been set upright, and has made fast every [t]hing above and below.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 5.56,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
        "has_bridge_connective": false,
        "bridge_phrase": null,
        "institutional_terms_found": [],
        "register_shift": true,
        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "words": 55,
      "text": "[The] second great and glorious rock is the new earth of light, which was set upon the earth of darkness. It has squashed the fastenings of the five storehouses of death. It has established firmness, with great firmness, over and beyond the earth of darkness. It has flattened, crushed and fixed the root of death.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 16.36,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
